            <ArticleTitle>Magnetic resonance imaging diagnosis of an aortocoronary saphenous vein graft aneurysm.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>330-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Magnetic resonance imaging (MRI) allowed the diagnosis of an atherosclerotic aneurysm of a long-standing aortocoronary saphenous vein graft, initially not depicted by selective coronary graft arteriography due to low flow within the lumen, caused by a stenosis of the proximal graft limb.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
